[2026-11-25T22:42:02Z] note: setup: library spec (original.md + ../../EXECUTION.md, ../../INDICATORS.md), Yahoo daily adjusted bars. - In-sample (tuning): 1995-01-01 → 2016-01-01; out-of-sample (validation only): 2016-01-01 → 2026-11-23 (frozen end) - Each symbol trades only after 400 bars of its own history - Capital 10,000 USD, 100% of equity per trade, fractional units - Fees 0.05% per side, slippage 0.03% per fill Part of SHARD2 of the 120-spec library, split across parallel sessions; runs only while holding one of logs/tso-slot-{1,2,3}.lock (max 3 optimizer containers machine-wide).
[2026-11-25T22:42:02Z] note: assumptions: - Position size = 100% of equity per trade, not the spec's risk_fraction sizing (user's choice for the library, so results compare on the leaderboard); risk_fraction is therefore not optimized. - Costs: fee 0.05% per side, slippage 0.03% per fill (repo US ETF/stock defaults, library-wide convention), slightly above the spec's 5 bp scenario. - Fills on adjusted prices (the project has no separate raw execution series). - In-sample 1995-01-01 → 2016-01-01, out-of-sample 2016-01-01 → 2026-11-23 (repo precedent for ETF strategies; same split across the library). - Indicators: EMA/RMA seeded with the SMA of the first n values, ATR = Wilder RMA of TR (INDICATORS.md). - Screening universe: Yahoo ETFs (spec: ETF); listed instruments are alternatives, tested separately. - Base symbol SPY (spec lists SPY, VTI; VTI is covered by the ETF screen). - Folder name golden_cross is the library spec; the older golden_cross_ws/_bl folders are separate experiments. - A cross is a one-bar event, so after an ATR stop/target/time exit the strategy waits for the next golden cross (literal reading of the spec).
[2026-11-25T22:42:02Z] note: backtest.py adapted from template: strategy block = CONFIG/PARAMS/SPACE/valid/signals plus shared indicator helpers (SMA-seeded EMA/RMA, Wilder ATR, crosses, memo cache). _simulate extended (machinery change, needed by the spec): ATR(14) of the signal bar frozen at entry for stop = E - stop_atr*A and target = E + take_profit_atr*A, entry skipped if A<=0/NaN or stop<=0; max_candles used as the time exit (max_bars); after an intrabar stop/target exit the next signal may come from the following bar on; run() applies the entry veto buy & ~sell. Gap fills and stop-before-target as in the template.
[2026-11-25T22:42:02Z] note: sanity check: defaults in-sample: 9 trades, 0.60%/yr, max DD -5.3%, win 66.7%, median 12 bars, exits {'target': 6, 'stop': 3}; out-of-sample: 5 trades, 0.59%/yr, max DD -6.2%, win 60.0%, median 19 bars, exits {'stop': 2, 'target': 3}. Verified all 9 in-sample default trades against the raw bars (buy true and sell false on the signal bar, entry fill = next open + slippage, stop/target levels from the frozen signal-bar ATR and not touched earlier, signal exits after a sell bar, time exits at max_candles): 0 mismatches. Sample trade 2006-08-30 -> 2006-09-27 target bars=19.
[2026-11-25T22:42:23Z] note: settings: min_trades_is 8 (default 20), min_trades_oos 3 (default 5), balanced_min_win_rate 40 (default 45), passed as flags on every run of this folder, because a 50/200 SMA cross trades about every 2 years (defaults: 9 IS trades on SPY) and a trend follower's normal win rate is 35-45%. Same reasoning as golden_cross_ws, slightly stricter.
